EmuFive: a GPU interrupt reached the guest before the label of the same end-of-pipe when that label
was handed to the GPU thread (a write-protected page with GPU-shared memory on). The guest woke,
read the old value and waited again for good: Invincible VS stopped with "GameThread timed out
waiting for RenderThread". Such an interrupt now goes through the GPU thread too, after the label.
Also: a command list blocked for 10 s logs what it waits for ("GPU queue N stuck for 10 s: ...").

